    <comment>- Update to 5.15.1:
  * Fix DFlash candidate-token device mismatch when models are
    split with device_map=&quot;auto&quot;
  * Align CandidateGenerator sampling with the processed logit
    distribution
  * Fix MTP config when mlp_layer_types is absent
  * Fall back from Lanczos to bicubic image resampling on CUDA
  * Move Gemma 4 video features onto the model device
</comment>
    <requestid>1372113</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>a17d31236ff6502d99816bc1a0af187b</srcmd5>
    <version>5.16.1</version>
    <time>1787849498</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-transformers to 5.16.1 (crosses 5.16.0).

New models: Qwen4-Exp, Granite Speech 5.0, Step-3.7-Flash, CohereCompass, ESMC,
ESMFold2 and GLM-5.3-Flash.

Breaking changes upstream declares for 5.16.0: the legacy tensor-parallel
implementation was replaced by a DTensor-native backend (5.16.1 restores
backwards compatibility for the old API with a deprecation cycle),
wav2vec2_conformer / wav2vec2-bert / SeamlessM4T-v2 now dispatch
attn_implementation=&quot;sdpa&quot;, and FuyuProcessor no longer returns
image_patch_indices.

transformers-allow-tokenizers-0.23.1.patch is dropped: upstream took the fix in
huggingface/transformers#46381 and now declares tokenizers &gt;=0.23.1,&lt;0.24.0
itself, so the downstream widening is obsolete. The Requires/BuildRequires floor
is raised to 0.23.1 to match; the &lt;0.24.0 ceiling stays declared so a future
0.24 shows up as unresolvable rather than installing and failing at import time.

Also converts the package from update-alternatives to libalternatives. Both
flavours ship /usr/bin/transformers as a real symlink to alts plus their own
priority conf under %{_datadir}/libalternatives/transformers/, and %pre carries
the update-alternatives migration. No other package provides that command name,
so there is no shared-command-pair sequencing to coordinate.

No CVE in the v5.15.1..v5.16.1 commit range (167 commits grepped for CVE ids).
CVE-2025-6921 / boo#1250447 is already cited in the 5.15.0 changelog entry and
is unaffected by this bump.

Built green locally on aarch64 against science:machinelearning/openSUSE_Tumbleweed;
the %check import smoke test passes for python313 and python314. rpmlint is
unchanged from the previous build at 4 badness (4x non-executable-script on
upstream's shebanged library modules, pre-existing). source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1373869</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
